From 85d3e40533e2c483d22c97a8aea94d4779615a19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:45:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] present: debanding option (off/low/high), 2D and 3D scenes

Smooths the colour steps of the PS2's 16-bit gradients with a sparse
edge-preserving average at the picture's own resolution (after the 2D filter),
then draws the float result with a +-0.45 LSB dither at window resolution so
it does not re-band at 8 bits. GA2_DEBAND=off|low|high, live from the F2 menu
and the launcher (new "Debanding" entry after PS2 dithering). Nothing runs
when off. Developer aids: GA2_DEBAND_STATS (GPU timer query),
GA2_DEBAND_SPLIT, GA2_DEBAND_DUMP. ga2_mpv::Chain::release() frees GL objects
(also used when the 2D filter changes).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
